  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 2,
   "text": "THE MECHANICS OF THE OSI BUMPER SPRING",
   "box": {
    "x": 230,
    "y": 920,
    "w": 980,
    "h": 50
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "1. The weight of the BHA attached above the Bumper Spring creates a downward force on the shear pin section of the tool. The shear pin section has three pins that shear at 9700 pounds of force.",
   "box": {
    "x": 251,
    "y": 991,
    "w": 533,
    "h": 76
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "2. When the pins shear, the perforated upper section falls into the lower section of the tool, where numerous stacked compression disks absorb the impact.",
   "box": {
    "x": 251,
    "y": 1091,
    "w": 533,
    "h": 76
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "3. The perforations in the upper section allow fluid to flow out releasing the pressure, in the housing, created by fluid accumulation.",
   "box": {
    "x": 251,
    "y": 1192,
    "w": 533,
    "h": 50
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "image",
   "src": "https://static.wixstatic.com/media/1ac9e9_9394f10118554b339cd3b3f97563a865~mv2.png/v1/fill/w_160,h_160,al_c,q_85,usm_0.66_1.00_0.01,enc_avif,quality_auto/BULL%20PLUG.png",
   "alt": "BULL PLUG.png",
   "natural": {
    "w": 160,
    "h": 160
   },
   "box": {
    "x": 1009,
    "y": 1209,
    "w": 160,
    "h": 160
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "4. The plunger forces fluid downward into the center tube.",
   "box": {
    "x": 251,
    "y": 1268,
    "w": 533,
    "h": 25
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "5. The fluid pushes back up creating a hydraulic force which decreases the velocity and lessens the impact.",
   "box": {
    "x": 251,
    "y": 1318,
    "w": 533,
    "h": 50
   }
  },
  {
